{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>רע</b> — a noun." "<b>וירוע</b> — of the pattern of תרועם. And likewise is <b>הוא שבר ישבר</b>: one who guarantees a stranger he does not know." "<b>ושונא</b> — who will strike a confident palm and does not fear the creditor."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "He identifies רע here as a noun (i.e., the object guaranteed), not the adjective 'bad' or the common noun 'friend/neighbor' he proceeds to distinguish from ירוע.", 1 "תרועם (Job 38:23) read as an abstract noun cognate with רוע; the second gloss quotes Prov 6:3, כי כן תציל את רעך וירוע, where Ibn Ezra parses ירוע as a noun (the guarantor) rather than as the standard verb 'and you shall guarantee.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:13.205322141Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}